# MyPA environment template — copy to .env and fill in.
# The app (one binary, `mypa --role=all|ingress|worker`, default all) and the audit worker validate
# their own keys at startup (internal/config/validate.go) and refuse to start, listing every
# missing/placeholder value, if something they need is absent. "app" below means the default role;
# a split install (V4-01) needs the ingress keys on its ingress and the rest on its worker.
# Legend:  [REQUIRED: services]   [CONDITIONAL: rule]   [optional]
# Generate secrets with:  openssl rand -hex 32

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Server / auth
# [optional] First household and its people, read ONCE: on a start with no household (a fresh
# install). Format: "phone_or_chat_id:Name:Role:FamilyGroup, ..." — one household per FamilyGroup
# (an entry without one gets a household of its own); a household without an admin makes its first
# entry admin. Once a household exists this setting is ignored (the start-up log and /doctor say
# so): add people with a pairing code from the dashboard instead (V4-30).
# An optional fifth field names the channel (telegram or whatsapp); without it a leading '+' is a
# WhatsApp number and anything else a Telegram ID (V4-32).
# Example: "+12025550101:Nivik:admin:MyFamily, 123456789:Jane:family:MyFamily:telegram"
ALLOWED_USERS=
# [REQUIRED: app] Bearer secret the dashboard uses to call /graphql.
DASHBOARD_API_SECRET=your-dashboard-api-secret
# [REQUIRED: app] The dashboard secret acts as an admin of THIS family group only
# (cannot read or change other families). Use the family group name from ALLOWED_USERS.
DASHBOARD_FAMILY_GROUP=your-family-group
# [REQUIRED: app] HMAC-SHA256 JWT signing secret. Must differ from ENCRYPTION_KEY.
JWT_SECRET=your-jwt-signing-secret
# [optional] Server secret that typed codes (/link codes, V4-32) are hashed under. It is kept out
# of the database and of backups, so a leaked database or backup cannot be searched for codes.
# Without it, linking a second app to a person (/link) is refused; everything else works.
# At least 32 characters, different from ENCRYPTION_KEY and JWT_SECRET. Codes that are still
# outstanding stop working after a restore onto an install with a different value.
# LINK_CODE_SECRET=
# [REQUIRED: app] AES-256-GCM key for OAuth tokens / API headers at rest.
# Changing it makes existing encrypted credentials unreadable (users must /connect again).
ENCRYPTION_KEY=your-32-byte-encryption-key

# [optional] debug|info|warn|error (default info). User message text is only logged at debug.
LOG_LEVEL=info
# [optional] Default IANA timezone for the assistant (e.g. Asia/Jerusalem); default UTC. A new
# household starts with it; a household's own time zone (dashboard API `updateHousehold`) wins.
DEFAULT_TIMEZONE=Asia/Jerusalem
# [optional] Household calendar conventions used in the system prompt.
WEEK_START_DAY=Sunday
WEEKEND_DAYS=Friday,Saturday

# [optional] The app's one HTTP port (webhooks, /graphql and Google sign-in). Default 8000.
# HTTP_PORT=8000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- How MyPA is reached (V4-40)
# The same release runs on a home PC or on a server; these settings choose, never file edits.
# [optional] INGRESS: how the outside world reaches this install. Default none.
#   none        nothing reaches it. Telegram polls for messages, so a Telegram-only install
#               needs no tunnel. WhatsApp needs a public address and refuses to start here.
#   caddy       a server with its own domain: the bundled Caddy gets the TLS certificate itself.
#               Ports 80 and 443 must reach the machine and the domain's DNS must point at it.
#   cloudflare  a Cloudflare Tunnel (set CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN below).
#   tailscale   Tailscale Funnel (set TAILSCALE_AUTHKEY below).
#   proxy       your own reverse proxy, forwarding to 127.0.0.1:8000 (nothing bundled runs).
#   ngrok       an ngrok tunnel (set NGROK_AUTHTOKEN below).
INGRESS=none
# [CONDITIONAL: app, when INGRESS is not none] The one public https address of this install, with
# no path. Every public address is derived from it: the Telegram webhook (/webhook/telegram), the
# WhatsApp webhooks (/webhook/twilio, /webhook/twilio/status) and the Google sign-in redirect
# (/auth/google/callback). On a domain you control it stays the same when the install moves
# between a home PC and a server, so nothing changes at Twilio or Google.
# Without it, Google sign-in returns to http://localhost:<HTTP_PORT>, which only works in a
# browser on this machine.
PUBLIC_URL=
# [CONDITIONAL] Starts the bundled tunnel or proxy: the profile named like INGRESS (ngrok,
# cloudflare, tailscale or caddy). Empty for none and proxy. Add "tools" for pgAdmin. The app
# refuses to start if it names another ingress's profile or misses the chosen one.
COMPOSE_PROFILES=
# [CONDITIONAL: INGRESS=cloudflare] The tunnel's token. In the Cloudflare dashboard, give the
# tunnel the public hostname of PUBLIC_URL and the service http://app:8000.
CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=
# [CONDITIONAL: INGRESS=tailscale] An auth key for the node. PUBLIC_URL is then
# https://<TAILSCALE_HOSTNAME>.<your tailnet>.ts.net (enable Funnel for the tailnet first).
TAILSCALE_AUTHKEY=
TAILSCALE_HOSTNAME=mypa
# [CONDITIONAL: INGRESS=ngrok] The agent's token. PUBLIC_URL is your reserved ngrok domain
# (there is no committed default).
NGROK_AUTHTOKEN=your-ngrok-authtoken

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Telegram
# [optional — enables Telegram] Bot token from @BotFather.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=your-telegram-bot-token
# With a public address (INGRESS and PUBLIC_URL) the app registers the webhook
# PUBLIC_URL/webhook/telegram with TELEGRAM_SECRET_TOKEN on startup. With INGRESS=none it polls.
# [CONDITIONAL: app, when TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN is set and there is a public address]
# 1-256 chars of A-Z a-z 0-9 _ -  (openssl rand -hex 32)
TELEGRAM_SECRET_TOKEN=your-telegram-webhook-secret-token

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Infrastructure URLs
# The three *_URL values below are ONLY for services run on the host (`go run ./cmd/mypa`), so
# they point at localhost (compose publishes the ports on 127.0.0.1). Inside Docker, compose
# ignores them and builds each URL from the *_USER/*_PASS/*_DB values plus the service name
# (rabbitmq, redis, postgres) — keep those credentials in sync with the URLs.
# [optional] Managed services (V4-40): an EXTERNAL_* address replaces the bundled container's
# inside Docker. The bundled container still starts but holds nothing. Empty = bundled.
EXTERNAL_DATABASE_URL=
EXTERNAL_REDIS_URL=
EXTERNAL_RABBITMQ_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- RabbitMQ
# [REQUIRED: app, audit-worker — host runs only, see above]
RABBITMQ_URL=amqp://<YOUR_RABBITMQ_USER>:<YOUR_RABBITMQ_PASSWORD>@localhost:5672/
# Used by the broker container and by every Docker service's RABBITMQ_URL.
RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_USER=<YOUR_RABBITMQ_USER>
RABBITMQ_DEFAULT_PASS=<YOUR_RABBITMQ_PASSWORD>
# [optional] Max concurrent conversation turns (different users run in parallel; one user's
# messages are always processed in order). Default 4.
RABBITMQ_PREFETCH=4

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Redis
# [REQUIRED: app — host runs only, see above]
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Database (PostgreSQL)
# [REQUIRED: app, audit-worker — host runs only, see above]
DATABASE_URL=postgres://<YOUR_DB_USER>:<YOUR_DB_PASSWORD>@localhost:5432/<YOUR_DB_NAME>?sslmode=disable
# Used by the postgres container and by every Docker service's DATABASE_URL.
POSTGRES_USER=<YOUR_DB_USER>
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=<YOUR_DB_PASSWORD>
POSTGRES_DB=<YOUR_DB_NAME>
# [optional] pgAdmin (opt-in: docker compose --profile tools up -d pgadmin). No default password.
PGADMIN_DEFAULT_EMAIL=<YOUR_PGADMIN_EMAIL>
PGADMIN_DEFAULT_PASSWORD=<YOUR_PGADMIN_PASSWORD>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Gemini
# [REQUIRED: app]
GEMINI_API_KEY=your-gemini-api-key
# [optional] The chat model. Leave it unset to use the built-in default, which is defined in one
# place (DefaultGeminiModel in internal/config/config.go; current value in SYSTEM.md section 8).
# GEMINI_MODEL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Optional integrations
# [optional] Tavily web search (search_web)
TAVILY_API_KEY=tvly-your_api_key_here
# [optional] Google OAuth for Calendar / Gmail / Tasks / Contacts
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-client-id
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-google-client-secret
# The redirect URI to register with Google is PUBLIC_URL/auth/google/callback (or
# http://localhost:8000/auth/google/callback with no public address).
# [optional] Groq Whisper voice transcription
GROQ_API_KEY=your-groq-api-key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Twilio (WhatsApp)
# [optional — enables WhatsApp]
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=your-twilio-account-sid
# [CONDITIONAL: app, when TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID is set]
# The app also rejects every WhatsApp webhook while this is empty.
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=your-twilio-auth-token
TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER=whatsapp:+14155238886
# WhatsApp needs a public address (INGRESS and PUBLIC_URL). Set PUBLIC_URL/webhook/twilio as the
# webhook in the Twilio console. Delivery reports go to PUBLIC_URL/webhook/twilio/status, so
# replies Twilio accepts but cannot deliver are logged at WARN with the error code.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Backups
# [recommended] age public key(s) to encrypt backups (generate: age-keygen -o backup.key).
# Empty = backups are written UNENCRYPTED.
BACKUP_AGE_RECIPIENTS=
# [restore only] path to the age private key; keep it off the server, mount only to restore.
BACKUP_AGE_IDENTITY_FILE=
